    <div class="t"><p>Greenery frames the windows of this ground-floor corner condominium at The Cove, where an extra large patio gives the home its own outdoor space. The open living area flows along a single run of wood flooring into the kitchen, beneath tall ceilings. A built-in wood shelf gives the living room its focal point, while recessed lighting and the glass door draw the eye toward the patio. The updated kitchen is the room everyone drifts toward. Quartz countertops, modern appliances and blue-gray cabinetry surround an oversized waterfall peninsula with plenty of counter space to prep, plate, and gather around for easy meals and connected conversations. Slide back the glass door and the day moves outside, ready for hosting friends or unwinding in private.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="u flip">
    <div class="pic"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/listings/401-crescent-ct-4101/home-2.jpg" alt="Bedroom with shuttered windows looking onto greenery"></div>
    <div class="t"><p>Storage starts at the front door with a coat closet and built-in shelving, and the generously sized bedroom follows suit with deep his and hers closets and efficient storage. The split bath adds flexibility, with a dual vanity and laundry closet in one room and the toilet and tub with shower in the other.</p><p>Gated Candlestick Point keeps daily routines conveniently close to home with a gym, a dog play area, a grill and picnic area, and 24/7 security. One deeded space and ample guest parking make arrivals simple. Nearby waterfront trails invite walks in the bay breeze and sunshine. A shuttle, free to community members, connects Balboa Park BART, Bayshore Caltrain and SFO for seamless transit to the city, the Peninsula, the East Bay and beyond. Drivers are just as well placed, with Highway 101 nearby. A one-bedroom that lives larger than it reads on paper, 401 Crescent Ct #4101 makes room for company and quiet alike.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

