      <div><p class="sub">What's planned</p><p>Construction began in September 2026 on the long-planned redevelopment of the former Candlestick Park stadium site, about half a mile away by road. The plan from the city and developer FivePoint calls for 7,200 homes, an innovation district with up to 2.8 million square feet of commercial space, shops, restaurants and a hotel across 270 acres. The first phase, about 700 homes, is expected in 2029, with the full build-out running into the 2040s.</p><p class="more"><a class="tlink" href="https://www.sf.gov/news-mayor-lurie-breaks-ground-on-7200-long-awaited-new-homes-at-former-candlestick-park-site" target="_blank" rel="noopener">More about the project and plans</a></p></div>
